      "message": "**Issue:** In `test_finger_capture_simple_image_scan_good`, you added the following comment and assertion:\n\n```cpp\n/* Assert no secondary FINGER_DOWN event was dispatched. */\nzassert_equal(\n    mkbp_send_event_fake.call_count, 2,\n    \"FINGER_DOWN should only trigger on the initial edge, not while held\");\n\n```\n\nBecause the implementation uses level-triggering (`st \u003d\u003d FINGER_PRESENT`) rather than edge-triggering, this comment is factually incorrect regarding the underlying behavior. The only reason a secondary `FINGER_DOWN` isn\u0027t dispatched in this specific test is because a `SCAN_GOOD` result immediately deactivates capture mode. In `test_finger_capture_simple_image_scan_too_fast`, capture mode remains active, and your test correctly expects the event to be spammed (verifying the continuous triggering).\n\n**Remediation:** Remove or rewrite the comment in `test_finger_capture_simple_image_scan_good` so it does not falsely claim the code is edge-triggered. It should instead clarify that no secondary event is dispatched because the capture session ended.",
